Chapter: AccpExperimentCard

Section: Guide

  mc-experiment-card : Text
  mc-experiment-card = "# ACCP experiments\n\nSelect library: experiment, including math and physics. Use output: json and print exactly one experiment-json object to expose result. Inspect execution status, result.status and result.convergence separately. Metadata is program-reported, not independently certified. A fact binds code and output, not a physical model's correctness.\n\n## Quantities\n\nquantity value symbol -> QuantityResult = QuantityValue (Quantity) | QuantityError (Text). Internally: finite binary64 SI magnitude and seven dimension exponents. quantity-add, quantity-sub, quantity-mul, quantity-div each take two QuantityResult values and propagate errors. Addition/subtraction reject unlike dimensions. quantity-in q symbol -> MathResult converts to compatible units. experiment-quantity q symbol assumptions -> ExperimentResult. Supported symbols: 1, rad, deg, m, cm, mm, km, ft, in, mi, kg, g, lb, s, min, h, A, K, mol, cd, m/s, km/h, mph, m/s^2, N, N/m, m^2, m^3, J, W, Pa, Hz, V, ohm. Other strings and affine Celsius/Fahrenheit are refused. Scalar physics APIs retain their SI conventions.\n\nChapter: UnitsExample\n  cites Accp chapter AccpExperiment\nSection: Entry\n  opening : [Console] Nothing = act\n    print-line-uni (experiment-json (experiment-quantity (quantity-add (quantity 3.0 \"ft\") (quantity 1.0 \"m\")) \"m\" [\"linear length conversion\"]))\n  end\nPage 1\n\n## Structured results\n\nexperiment-scalar math-result unit method assumptions -> ExperimentResult. experiment-json result -> Text. ExperimentResult = ExperimentValue (ExperimentData) (ExperimentMeta) | ExperimentError (Text) (ExperimentMeta). JSON schema accp-experiment-1: status, value array or null, labels, units, method, tolerance array or null, refinement_difference array or null, convergence, assumptions, axis, axis_unit, settings, coordinates and samples (row-major). Errors have no usable value or partial samples. not_converged retains the fine trajectory but does not satisfy requested tolerance. Agreement is not a certified solution-error bound. Decimal fields are approximate previews. The binary64 object carries exact signed 64-bit bit patterns as decimal strings for value, coordinates, samples, tolerance and refinement_difference; use those for lossless replay and precise comparisons. Settings include initial_binary64 and interval_binary64.\n\n## Coupled ODE\n\nexperiment-ode f t0 initial t1 steps stride labels units tolerances assumptions -> ExperimentResult. f : Real, List Real -> List Real; time is seconds. The callback receives a fresh state list and must return a finite derivative vector of the same length. initial and tolerances are List Real; labels, units and assumptions are List Text. Component units are conventions, not inferred dimensions of callback equations. Tolerances are positive finite absolute values in component units.\n\nOne to eight components; one to 1024 coarse steps; fine run doubles steps and sampling stride. Stride divides coarse steps. Samples include both endpoints: steps/stride + 1, at most 256 samples and 1024 scalar cells. Published values/samples come from the fine run. Differences are maxima across corresponding retained samples; refinement_passed requires every difference <= tolerance. Backward intervals are supported. Equal endpoints return the initial state once without callback evaluation, convergence not_applicable. Invalid vectors, nonfinite states or unrepresentable steps are errors. User callbacks can mutate their own captured objects; reproducibility requires a deterministic callback.\n\nChapter: Oscillator\n  cites Accp chapter AccpExperiment\nSection: Model\n  oscillator : Real, List Real -> List Real\n  oscillator (t) (y) = [list-at y 1, -4.0 * list-at y 0 - 0.4 * list-at y 1]\nSection: Entry\n  opening : [Console] Nothing = act\n    print-line-uni (experiment-json (experiment-ode oscillator 0.0 [1.0,0.0] 8.0 256 4 [\"position\",\"velocity\"] [\"m\",\"m/s\"] [0.00001,0.00001] [\"mass 1 kg, stiffness 4 N/m, damping 0.4 kg/s\"]))\n  end\nPage 1\n\nRun with library experiment, output json, limits.ms 10000. Settings retain initial state, endpoints, step counts and coarse stride. Preserve submitted source, callback and returned fact for reproduction; journals retain hashes, not source.\n\n## Sweeps\n\nexperiment-sweep f parameters parameter-unit value-unit assumptions -> ExperimentResult; f : Real -> MathResult. One to 256 finite parameters, preserved in caller order including duplicates. An invalid point fails the whole sweep. value is the final row, coordinates contain inputs, samples contain singleton output rows. convergence is not_checked.\n\n## SVG\n\nexperiment-svg result component -> ExperimentPlot = PlotSvg (Text) | PlotError (Text). Component is zero-based. Match both arms and print PlotSvg text with default output text for export. Arbitrary stdout is never automatically rendered. Invalid results, scalars without samples and invalid components fail. Nonconverged plots carry not_converged in the title. Fixed 800 by 480 SVG; x increases rightward, y upward; segments follow sample order. Constant ranges pad by max(1,abs(value)*0.05) in declared units. No plot unit conversion. Unrepresentable ranges fail. XML-escaped labels, no scripts or external resources. Saving is a caller action.\n\nExisting source, output, memory and time ceilings remain. The bundle consumes part of the 64 KiB source allowance. ODE work/allocation is proportional to steps times components plus callback cost; retained samples to samples times components. Full contract: apps/accp/experiments.md."

